      "side": 1,
      "message": "I highly recommend swapping the order of these algorithms:\n\n```\n      KeyAlgoRSA, KeyAlgoRSASHA512,\n```\n\nWhen we put these changes in production, we noticed a number of clients would fail with RSA keys, and the server would report:\n\n```\nsignature \"ssh-rsa\" not compatible with selected algorithm \"rsa-sha2-512\"\n``` \n\nAs https://adamheins.com/blog/ssh-agent-key-rsa mentions, older gpg-agent versions do not support `rsa-sha2-512`. On Ubuntu 18.04, which uses gpg-agent v2.2.4 and OpenSSH v7.6, logins that use RSA keys that use gpg-agent (e.g. Yubikey keys) will fail unless `ssh-rsa` takes precedence over `rsa-sha2-512`.\n\nUpgrading gpg-agent appears to solve the problem, but OpenSSH puts `ssh-rsa` first.",
